.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-2-Clause
.Dd October 7, 2026
.Dt NDPKG-SYSTEM 8
.Os NeoDarwin
.Sh NAME
.Nm ndpkg system
.Nd upgrade and roll back the base system as ZFS boot environments
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm ndpkg
.Op Fl r Ar repo ...
.Cm system upgrade
.Op Ar version
.Nm ndpkg
.Cm system status
.Op Fl -json
.Nm ndpkg
.Cm system list | confirm | rollback
.Nm ndpkg
.Cm boot
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The base system \(em the kernel collection and the userland base \(em is a
.Em system set :
a signed package of kind
.Li system-set
whose requirements pin its components exactly
.Pq Li "name = version" :
one
.Li kernel-collection
package, carrying
.Pa /System/Library/Kernels/kernelcache
and the static trust cache that goes with it, and
.Li system
packages.
Each ZFS boot environment (BE) holds one set, with the receipts of its
packages in
.Pa /System/Library/Receipts/ndpkg/ Ns Ar name .
.Pp
The boot loader reads kernels from the EFI System Partition, so
.Nm
keeps a mirror of the ESP in
.Pa /var/db/ndpkg/system/esp ,
on the
.Li POOL/pkg
dataset every BE shares, with each BE's kernel collection and trust cache in
.Pa NeoDarwin/be/ Ns Ar BE ,
and writes the ESP from it whole.
.Bl -tag -width rollback
.It Cm upgrade Op Ar version
Finds the newest
.Pq or the given
version of the booted set in the repositories, verifies it and every
component, creates a BE
.Ar set Ns - Ns Ar version
from the booted one
.Pq Xr ndbectl 8 ,
installs the components into it with their receipts, puts its kernel on the
ESP and makes it boot once
.Pq Pa \eNeoDarwin\ebootonce ,
which the loader deletes as it boots it.
Reboot to try it.
.It Cm confirm
Run at every boot by
.Cm ndpkg boot .
If the booted BE is the pending try, it becomes the default (the pool's
.Li bootfs
and the ESP's
.Li be= ) ,
and the old default is kept for
.Cm rollback .
If another BE booted, the try failed: the loader fell back to the default.
.It Cm rollback
Makes the BE the last change replaced the default again.
.It Cm status
The booted BE and its set, the default, a pending try, the rollback target
and the booted set's packages.
.It Cm list
Each BE with flags
.Li N
(booted),
.Li D
(the default),
.Li T
(tried once at the next boot),
.Li P
(the rollback target), and the set it was made with.
.It Cm boot
The launchd job
.Pa org.neodarwin.ndpkg.boot :
mounts
.Li POOL/pkg ,
loads the booted set's packages' trust caches, restores installed packages
.Pq Cm ndpkg activate ,
then runs
.Cm system confirm .
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width indent -compact
.It Pa /var/db/ndpkg/system/state
.Li previous
and
.Li try
.It Pa /var/db/ndpkg/system/sets/ Ns Ar BE
the set a BE was made with
.It Pa /var/db/ndpkg/system/esp
the ESP's mirror
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr ndbectl 8 ,
.Xr ndpkg 8
.Sh HISTORY
P2-03.
It replaces
.Xr freebsd-update 8 ,
.Xr etcupdate 8
and
.Xr freebsd-version 1
.Pq Cm ndpkg system status .
Kernel extensions come only inside a set's kernel collection package for
now; packages of single kexts and the auxiliary collection are not built.
